<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    FocusGuard — res/values/colors.xml
    ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    Color Philosophy:
      A wellbeing app must feel calm, trustworthy, and non-alarming.
      Research on digital health UX shows that:
        - Muted purples/indigos reduce anxiety vs. aggressive reds
        - Soft greens reinforce positive "focused" states
        - Warm ambers signal caution without panic (better than pure red)
        - High-contrast text on mid-tone surfaces improves readability

    This palette uses Material Design 3's tonal system:
      Primary   → Soft indigo/violet  (calm focus, trust)
      Secondary → Muted teal          (serenity, balance)
      Tertiary  → Warm amber          (gentle warning)
      Error     → Muted rose          (softer than harsh red)

    All colors are defined as both light and dark variants.
    Dynamic color (Android 12+) will override these with wallpaper-based
    tones automatically — these are the static fallbacks.
    ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-->
<resources>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         PRIMARY — Soft Indigo (calm focus, brand identity)
         ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
